description.en:
Recruits a character into the player's roster, by player parameter ID, and returns the new player's handle.
This is the low-level native behind the ev_main helper AddParty and all its message wrappers.

What happens:
- the ID is hashed and looked up in the player parameter table; an unknown ID returns 0;
- if the roster is already full (the retail game caps it at 112 players), the call returns 0. Characters that carry a particular flag in their parameter data skip this check, except para_cp0012, para_cp0013 and para_cp0014, which are always checked;
- if the character is already in the roster pool but marked as having left, it is simply brought back and keeps its handle;
- otherwise a new player record is created and added to the roster.

examples.code:
// Add the character, then lock its slot, disable its Fighting Spirit
// and set its level, only if the recruitment worked.
local hdl = CMND_ADD_PARTY("para_cp0008");
if (hdl > 0)
{
	CMND_SET_PT_LOCK_FLAG(hdl, true);
	CMND_SET_AVATAR_ENABLE(hdl, false);
	CMND_SET_AVATAR_LOCK_FLAG(hdl, false);
	CMND_SET_LV(hdl, 5);
}
